1
00:00:00,460 --> 00:00:05,430
Rome fell in 476. Then it fell again,
nine hundred and seventy-seven years

2
00:00:05,480 --> 00:00:06,780
later.

3
00:00:07,060 --> 00:00:12,140
In 395 the emperor Theodosius dies,
and his sons split the empire:

4
00:00:12,190 --> 00:00:17,096
a western half ruled from Italy, an
eastern half from Constantinople.

5
00:00:17,416 --> 00:00:23,656
The West lasts eighty-one years. In 476
a general named Odoacer deposes its last

6
00:00:23,706 --> 00:00:29,250
emperor, a boy called Romulus Augustulus.
That's the date in the textbooks.

7
00:00:29,510 --> 00:00:34,250
But the eastern half doesn't fall. It
goes on calling itself the Roman Empire

8
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:38,550
for nearly a thousand years, until the
Ottomans take Constantinople on the

9
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:41,350
twenty-ninth of May, 1453.

10
00:00:41,710 --> 00:00:45,490
From Romulus to the last Constantine:
twenty-two centuries of Rome,

11
00:00:45,540 --> 00:00:47,473
on one line you can zoom.

12
00:00:47,763 --> 00:00:50,172
That's OpenChronology, and it's free.
